window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["38"]={"https://theconversation.com/humidity-can-make-heatwaves-more-dangerous-its-time-to-warn-australians-about-this-threat-295453":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"e8310068cbe2b25da024d305240d781f629698ad9be16904d9012b49ad6d3925","read":"https://theconversation.com/humidity-can-make-heatwaves-more-dangerous-its-time-to-warn-australians-about-this-threat-295453","bytes":188428,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Humidity can make heatwaves more dangerous. It’s time to warn Australians about this threat","by":[{"n":"Alyson Wright","r":"Adjunct Fellow in Public Health, Menzies School of Health Research"},{"n":"Mark de Souza","r":"PhD Candidate in Sustainable Healthcare, The University of Melbourne"},{"n":"Sharon Campbell","r":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Environmental Health Research, University of Tasmania"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T22:18:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It’s the build-up in northern Australia – the time of year when heat and humidity get worse ahead of the wet season. Common phrases such as “going troppo” or “ ",["mango madness","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-12-30/mango-madness/104703932"],"” give a sense of the effects. Tempers fray and tensions rise."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s now ",["emerging evidence","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-026-48668-z"]," that humidity makes heat more dangerous. ",["Humid heatwaves","https://www.aspi.org.au/report/lethal-humidity-and-the-systemic-risks-of-climate-change/"]," – where high temperatures combine with high humidity – are potentially more dangerous than dry heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elsewhere in the world, humid heatwaves are already claiming lives. Over 1,300 pilgrims died in Saudi Arabia in 2024 due to lethal levels of ",["humidity and heat","https://theconversation.com/more-than-1-300-hajj-pilgrims-died-this-year-when-humidity-and-heat-pushed-past-survivable-limits-its-just-the-start-245271"],", while ",["India and Pakistan","https://theconversation.com/too-hot-too-humid-why-the-sustained-heatwave-in-india-and-pakistan-is-so-dangerous-283762"]," have also been hard hit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["recent research","https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GH001562"]," in the Northern Territory found more people came to emergency departments during intense humid heatwaves than comparable dry heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is, we’re not warning people about this combined threat. Australia’s heatwave warning systems focus only on temperature – not on humidity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why humidity matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Intense heat stresses the body. Humidity can make this worse."]},{"k":"p","s":["The human body relies heavily on sweating to regulate temperature. When sweat evaporates from the skin, it removes heat and helps keep the body cool. When ",["humidity is high","https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-02461-6"],", evaporation doesn’t work as well and it’s harder for the body to release heat and stay cool."]},{"k":"p","s":["Humid conditions can boost the risk of heat-related illnesses such as heatstroke, worsen existing heart and lung conditions and put more strain on the bodies of people with chronic diseases."]},{"k":"p","s":["High humidity can also contribute to poor sleep, reducing the body’s ability to recover during prolonged hot periods."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hot and wet conditions also provide optimal conditions for mosquitoes, ticks and parasites, which are vectors for the spread of ",["key tropical diseases","https://theconversation.com/murray-valley-encephalitis-can-be-fatal-with-no-vaccine-heres-how-to-stay-safe-283573"],". Mould, bacteria and viruses are more likely to grow in high humidity, increasing the risk of ",["lung and skin disease","https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24119456"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What we found in the Northern Territory"]},{"k":"p","s":["The top third of the Northern Territory has a monsoonal coastal climate prone to humidity, while the two thirds inland is arid. This means we can analyse and compare humid and dry heatwaves across these environments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study ",["analysed","https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GH001562"]," more than two decades of emergency department data across the NT to see if dry heat or humid heat affected the numbers of people needing emergency care. We used a ",["temperature-based index","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cliser.2022.100315"]," for dry heat and a combined temperature and relative humidity index to determine humid heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["The results were clear. While more people sought emergency treatment during both dry and humid heatwaves, humid heatwaves were worse. Severe and extreme dry heatwaves led to 4.4% more hospital visits, while similar humid heatwaves saw 6.1% more people attending emergency departments."]},{"k":"p","s":["When arid areas of the Territory were hit by humid heatwaves, the effect was even clearer – emergency visits rose 8.7%."]},{"k":"h","s":["Where are the warnings?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In many parts of northern Australia, heatwaves ",["are projected","https://environment.nt.gov.au/media/docs/climate-change-response/state-of-the-science-and-climate-change-impacts-final-report.pdf"]," to become more frequent and intense due to global warming."]},{"k":"p","s":["Every summer, Australia’s Bureau of Meteorology issues ",["heatwave warnings","https://www.bom.gov.au/news-and-media/heatwaves-what-you-need-to-know"]," to give people advance notice of three or more days of unusual heat over day and night. Warnings can be issued for mild, severe and extreme heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["These warnings are vital. They let people prepare for heat and change plans, while health services can boost staffing numbers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is, these warnings are largely based on ",["temperature","https://www.bom.gov.au/weather-and-climate/specialised-forecasts-and-observations/heatwave"],". Most people can tolerate a 35°C day with low humidity. But a 35°C day with high humidity is much harder for us to cope with."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means the current system may not be warning Australians about a real risk to their health – especially those in tropical and coastal regions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Preparing health services for humid heat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Health services in the NT are often ageing and ",["under strain","https://doi.org/10.1111/ajr.12858"],". Last wet season did ",["significant damage","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-28/katherine-hospital-calls-for-relocation-after-flood-evacuations/106501586"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dry and wet heatwaves will put more pressure on health systems already struggling during ",["extreme weather","https://www.insidestategovernment.com.au/nt-health-confirms-system-wide-pressures-amid-weather-crisis/"],". Even a modest increase in patients will add more pressure on staffing, bed capacity and resources."]},{"k":"p","s":["We’ve long known heat affects some people much more than others. Children, older adults, people with chronic diseases and those in disadvantaged communities are hit harder. In the Territory, ",["low-quality housing","https://doi.org/10.3390/architecture4030041"],", ",["poor access to healthcare","https://doi.org/10.1071/AH21276"]," and ",["outdoor work and recreation","https://doi.org/10.3390/su142113805"]," also boost risks from heat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Time to redefine heatwaves"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s ",["no longer enough","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cliser.2022.100315"]," to define a heatwave using temperature alone. Across northern Australia, humidity directly affects how people experience a heatwave."]},{"k":"p","s":["Climatologists are already ",["exploring ways","https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/adc1e5"]," to include humidity in measures of dangerous heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["To take the threat of humid heat seriously, we need to redefine heatwaves to include humidity and temperature. This will strengthen our ",["early warning systems","https://doi.org/10.1007/s40572-025-00496-5"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On a practical level, we need to prepare our health systems for more demand during severe humid heat, particularly in remote and tropical regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the Top End prepares for another wet season, authorities will focus on the threats of cyclones, flooding and other visible weather threats. It’s time to look at a less visible danger – the combination of heat and humidity."]}],"chars":5084},"https://theconversation.com/us-democrats-win-final-two-senate-seats-coalition-likely-to-easily-win-victorian-election-296423":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6e8040ed0b3280a00ea9a774691821e762ea70ec4dfccfd09d3ed133afad2b96","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-democrats-win-final-two-senate-seats-coalition-likely-to-easily-win-victorian-election-296423","bytes":181636,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US Democrats win final two Senate seats; Coalition likely to easily win Victorian election","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-15T23:05:47Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the United States, Democrats have won the final two undecided Senate seats at the midterms to take an overall 56–44 Senate majority over Republicans. Democrats are likely to win the House of Representatives by 260–175."]},{"k":"p","s":["With 12 days to go until the November 28 Victorian election, a Redbridge poll has the Coalition leading Labor by 57–43 after preferences. The Coalition is likely to easily win a majority of the 88 lower house seats in its own right."]},{"k":"p","s":["The New South Wales election is in March 2027. With NSW using optional preferential voting, the split in the One Nation/Coalition vote in the Resolve poll helps Labor."]},{"k":"h","s":["US Democrats win final two Senate seats"]},{"k":"p","s":["All 435 United States federal House of Representatives seats and 35 of the 100 Senate seats were up for election at November 3 midterm elections. In the 2024 elections, Republicans won the House by 220–215 over the Democrats and the Senate by 53–47."]},{"k":"p","s":["I wrote for ",["The Poll Bludger","https://www.pollbludger.net/2026/11/14/us-mid-term-elections-late-counting-thread-2/"]," on Saturday that Democrat Mary Peltola is certain to win the Alaska Senate contest, defeating Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan. Last Thursday AEDT, the Mississippi Senate contest was called for Democrat Scott Colom, who defeated Republican incumbent Cindy Hyde-Smith."]},{"k":"p","s":["Donald Trump won Mississippi by nearly 23 points at the 2024 presidential election, and the last Democrat to win that state’s Senate contest was in 1982, when southern Democrats were still regarded as racist. The previous Mississippi Democratic senator, John Stennis, was a “ ",["zealous supporter of racial segregation","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Stennis"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["These wins give Democrats a 56–44 Senate majority over Republicans, gaining nine seats at the midterm elections. Seven of Democrats’ gains occurred in states Trump won by ",["double-digit margins","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election#Results_by_state"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the ",["House of Representatives","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/11/03/us/elections/results-house.html"],", Democrats lead Republicans in called races by 256–169 with ten still undecided. Democrats are likely to win by 260–175, the largest Democratic ",["majority since the 1991–93 Congress","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party_divisions_of_United_States_Congresses"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the ",["Cook Political Report’s tracker","https://www.cookpolitical.com/vote-tracker/2026/house"],", Democrats are winning the national popular vote by 56.2–42.3, a 13.9-point margin, compared with a 2.6-point ",["Republican margin in 2024","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I said in the Poll Bludger article that Democrats’ 59.8% of expected House seats is an underperformance of their popular vote margin in single-member systems. Republican gerrymanders probably prevented more losses, although the Republican gerrymander of North Carolina backfired spectacularly."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Redbridge poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["Redbridge and Accent Research poll","https://www.afr.com/politics/victorian-coalition-position-strengthens-labor-reduced-to-rump-in-new-poll-20261111-p61d0z"]," for The Financial Review, conducted November 3–10 from a sample of 1,008, gave the Coalition 31% of the primary vote (up one since the early October Redbridge poll), Labor 23% (down one), One Nation 22% (down two), the Greens 15% (down one) and all Others 9% (up three)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition was at its highest since December 2025, while Labor and One Nation were at their lowest since August. The Greens were one point off their October high."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, the Coalition led Labor by 57–43, a one-point gain for the Coalition. Labor led One Nation by 55–45."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor Premier Ben Carroll’s net favourability was down ten points to -28 (47% unfavourable, 19% favourable). Liberal leader Jess Wilson’s was down ten points to +7 (35% favourable, 28% unfavourable). One Nation leader Warren Pickering’s was down three points to -8 (25% unfavourable, 17% favourable). Greens leader Ellen Sandell’s was down one point to -3 (13% unfavourable, 10% favourable)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 29% (up one), Carroll 18% (down one) and Pickering 11% (up three)."]},{"k":"p","s":["On whether the Coalition had done enough to deserve to win the next election, respondents gave a -4 net agree score, up four points since October and up 15 points since June 2025. But on whether Labor had done enough, they gave a net -43 agree score, down eight points since October. In the poll before Ben Carroll replaced Jacinta Allan as premier in late July, Labor had a net agree of -50."]},{"k":"p","s":["All recent polls show swings to the Coalition, and the Coalition now has a big lead over Labor as the graph below shows."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Lighthouse poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["The second instalment of the ",["Victorian Lighthouse poll","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/time-for-a-change-coalition-extends-lead-over-labor-as-premier-ben-carroll-faces-losing-his-seat/news-story/5b54bdde2fb1c75512f1ab7a4a448fc3"]," for The Herald Sun gave the Coalition 32% of the primary vote (up one since the ",["Lighthouse poll published November 6","https://theconversation.com/poor-polls-continue-for-both-federal-and-victorian-labor-295756"],"), One Nation 23% (steady), Labor 21% (down one), the Greens 14% (steady) and all Others 10% (steady)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll’s net favourability was up two points to -19, while Wilson’s surged eight points to +17."]},{"k":"p","s":["This poll is being conducted internally by News Corp. No fieldwork dates were provided, but the sample size was 1,351. There will be weekly updates of this poll until the election."]},{"k":"h","s":["Upper house question from previous DemosAU poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["All 40 Victorian upper house members will be elected in eight five-member regions using preferences. A quota for election is one-sixth of the vote or 16.7%, with half a quota enough to give a reasonable chance of election."]},{"k":"p","s":["I previously ",["wrote about the DemosAU poll","https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132"]," that gave Labor just 18% of the primary vote in the lower house. In the ",["upper house","https://demosau.com/wp-content/uploads/DemosAU/vic-poll-nov-2026.html"],", voting intentions were 28% Coalition, 20% One Nation, 17% Labor, 15% Greens, 4% Animal Justice, 4% Family First and 4% Legalise Cannabis."]},{"k":"h","s":["NSW Resolve poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["The New South Wales election is in March 2027. A ",["Resolve poll","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/nsw/the-key-issues-giving-minns-an-edge-four-months-out-from-election-20261113-p61diu.html"]," for The Sydney Morning Herald, conducted with the October and November federal Resolve polls from a sample of 1,100, gave Labor 30% of the primary vote (up one since the September poll), One Nation 26% (up one), the Coalition 23% (down one), the Greens 13% (up two), independents 5% (steady) and others 3% (down two)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a record high in Resolve’s NSW polls for One Nation and the Greens’ highest vote since July 2025, while the Coalition is at an equal record low (tied with July)."]},{"k":"p","s":["No two-party estimate was provided, but ",["analyst Kevin Bonham estimated","https://x.com/kevinbonham/status/2121215834836381937"]," that Labor led the Coalition by over 57–43, with Labor vs One Nation “probably modestly closer”. NSW’s optional preferential voting helps Labor with the One Nation and Coalition vote split."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Labor incumbent Chris Minns had 30% (up three), Liberal leader Kellie Sloane 12% (down three) and One Nation state leader Mike Newman 11% (up three)."]}],"chars":6173},"https://theconversation.com/what-bill-c-39s-loosened-environmental-regulations-could-mean-for-canadians-294851":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"800477aa7241914a3499e03f4c140bd642c39962f36c6598ff0dc5c29ed9b1d0","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-bill-c-39s-loosened-environmental-regulations-could-mean-for-canadians-294851","bytes":183941,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What Bill C-39’s loosened environmental regulations could mean for Canadians","by":[{"n":"Kerry Black","r":"Executive Co-Director, UNU Hub on Empowering Communities to Adapt to Environmental Change, Institute for Water, Environment and Health, United Nations University; University of Calgary"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T14:34:34Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Protests ",["took place","https://globalnews.ca/video/12148696/nationwide-protests-against-bill-c-39-hit-new-brunswick/"]," in cities across Canada today against a proposed bill that some fear could undermine environmental protections as well as the rights of workers and Indigenous communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian government introduced ",["Bill C-39","https://www.parl.ca/legisinfo/en/bill/45-1/c-39"],", the Building Canada Strong Act, in September 2026, with the stated aim of fast-tracking large-scale projects. Hailed as a major advancement by the government, ",["it has also been criticized as a bill that could bulldoze environmental regulations","https://thenarwhal.ca/canada-bill-c-39-environmental-assessments/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has said the proposed legislation is aimed at ",["protecting “economic security.”","https://www.winnipegfreepress.com/breakingnews/2026/09/28/canada-resorting-to-its-tried-and-true-playbook"]," Under the new bill, ",["new “federal economic zones” would be created where projects could be “pre-approved.”","https://thenarwhal.ca/canada-major-projects-economic-zones-proposal/"]," This would provide exceptions to habitat and species-at-risk protections and other federal oversight."]},{"k":"p","s":["What could this new legislation mean for environmental regulations and how could it impact Canadians if passed into law?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Less time for environmental review"]},{"k":"p","s":["In October 2024, the government released a framework for implementing the right to a healthy environment under the Canadian Environmental Protection Act, ",["linking environmental protection directly to human health and well-being","https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/news/2024/10/strengthening-protections-from-pollution-and-the-right-to-a-healthy-environment.html"],". However, Bill C-39 reduces the time period for thorough environmental review."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has touted the bill’s shortened timeline for project approval, ",["compressed to a one-year review","https://mcmillan.ca/insights/publications/bill-c-39-the-building-canada-strong-act-introduces-significant-reforms-to-federal-project-review-and-permitting-process/"],". This allows for quick decisions to be made, and proponents to know whether a specific project will be able to proceed in a shorter timeframe. While this is viewed as a clear advantage, some are warning that the ",["one-year timeline could still be extended and delayed","https://nationalpost.com/opinion/jamie-sarkonak-carneys-one-project-one-year-mirage"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Environmental regulations are not simply environmental protections, they also protect public health. Effective regulations reduce exposure to polluted air, contaminated water, toxic chemicals and climate-related hazards."]},{"k":"p","s":["They help prevent disease, improve quality of life, reduce health-care costs and protect the well-being of current and future generations. ",["Recent evidence shows","https://doi.org/10.1186/s41256-024-00373-y"]," that the health and economic benefits of environmental regulation far outweigh the relative costs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Build first, assess later"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Bill C-39, the government would be able to permit preliminary construction to begin before the Impact Assessment Agency of Canada completes an assessment. This would be the case if the environment minister considers a project to be in the ",["“public interest.”","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/building-canada-strong-c39-expert-environmental-concerns-9.7357425"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Reduced environmental regulations would directly impact the communities within the area of the proposed projects and those downstream. It could mean potential environmental ",["degradation and destruction, as well as weakened habitat protection, before a full assessment can be done","https://www.greenpeace.org/canada/en/press-release/76045/greenpeace-canada-reacts-to-the-introduction-of-bill-c-39-the-bulldoze-nature-bill/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of the proposed “projects of public interest” are in areas of significant ecological importance. Many are situated on or near First Nations territories. Leaders from the Nishnawbe Aski Nation stated they “will not accept this legislation as it stands,” stating they support responsible development but ",["that acceleration of development cannot be at the expense of Indigenous communities","https://www.nan.ca/news/nan-chiefs-reject-building-canada-strong-act/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government is wrong in assuming the choice is either environmental protection or rapid development. Many jurisdictions have shown that ",["projects can move faster","https://climateinstitute.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Regulatory-Reform-NRCAN-and-PCO-Nov.-13.2023.pdf"]," when governments improve co-ordination across departments and agencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["This could include digitizing permitting, establishing clear timelines, conducting strategic planning earlier and eliminating duplication in approval processes. The ",["evidence suggests that delays often arise","https://energy.ec.europa.eu/topics/renewable-energy/enabling-framework-renewables_en"]," from fragmented governance and administrative inefficiencies, not environmental safeguards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pay now, worry later"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bill C-39 also introduces changes to the ",["Fisheries Act","https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/f-14/"]," that make it easier to advance projects that may impact fish or fish habitats. The bill introduces third-party “habitat credits” and fees for minor impacts. Under this model, a third party can engage in habitat restoration and effectively “sell” credits to companies building major projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["The bill would allow companies that damage fish habitat during construction to buy habitat restoration credits from approved conservation groups instead of doing the restoration work themselves. The goal is to speed up project approvals while still requiring companies to compensate for environmental damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Supporters say this could fund larger and ",["more effective habitat restoration projects","https://blog.cwf-fcf.org/index.php/en/cwf-welcomes-government-move-to-protect-fish-habitats/"],", reducing red tape without comprising environmental monitoring. Critics worry it could make it easier for ",["companies to damage fish habitats","https://www.nationalobserver.com/2026/10/01/news/feds-c39-habitat-loss-offsets-questioned"]," as long as they can afford to pay for credits elsewhere, allowing habitat damage to become simply a cost of doing business."]},{"k":"p","s":["Media coverage of Bill C-39 tends to focus on pipelines, mines and regulatory processes. However, it’s also about the air Canadians breathe and the water they drink. It is about the fish we catch and the natural spaces that support our health and well-being."]},{"k":"p","s":["The question is not whether Canada should build new projects or strengthen its economy. It must. The real question is whether it can do so without weakening environmental safeguards that protect communities, ecosystems and future generations."]},{"k":"p","s":["As governments push to accelerate development, Canadians should pay close attention. The consequences will be felt not only in boardrooms and construction sites. They will be felt in rivers, forests and households across the country for decades to come."]}],"chars":5361},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"5e391c5bc6f849158ca4f1c8b9316b246c0fffbace5d4699ff6a2763fcf8edea","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/greece","bytes":114833,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Greece travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-03T11:18:20+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Winter weather in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece can experience severe weather over the winter period, including storms which can lead to flash flooding. For further advice, see the ‘Extreme weather and natural disasters’ section on the ",["Safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Greece’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Greece set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Greek Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/the-embassy"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Greece, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period without a visa. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-greece-for-work"]," are different. If you are a touring creative, see ",["details about the Uniform (Schengen) visa","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/visa.html?mission=lon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["For a longer stay, you must ",["apply to the Greek authorities for a national visa","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/visa.html?mission=lon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Greece with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-greece#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Greek implementation of EES"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greek authorities have indicated that they will not collect biometric data (fingerprints and photos) for UK travellers as part of EES. Follow the advice of authorities on the ground. If you are resident in Greece, make sure to show your residence documentation at passport control to ensure you are not registered in EES."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccines, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Greece guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Greece","https://www.aade.gr/en/customs"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques at your point of entry into Greece if you are carrying a value of 10,000 euros or more. You will be asked to complete the relevant declaration forms provided to you by the Customs Authorities. You should request a certified copy of the declaration to keep with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave. You can read further detail on the website of the Greek ",["Independent Authority for Public Revenue","https://www.aade.gr/en/greeks-abroad-non-residents/cash-reserves"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Greece."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several attacks involving explosives and automatic weapons against Greek institutions, shopping malls, banks, media offices, diplomatic premises and the police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 1 July 2026, three improvised incendiary device attacks against the residential properties of Greek political figures killed one person, with four others being injured"]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Political protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greek authorities have increased security at some prominent locations, including tourist sites, due to events in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently a heightened risk of such protests, particularly in central Athens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, stay away from protests and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Strikes and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular strikes, sometimes called at short notice, that can cause disruption to buses, trains, ferries and air travel, as well as road networks and borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations often take place around major squares in central Athens, in particular Syntagma Square. Political demonstrations may take place on certain dates:"]},{"k":"li","s":["1 May (Labour Day)"]},{"k":"li","s":["17 November (anniversary of when student protests against a military dictatorship were put down violently – ‘Polytechnio’)"]},{"k":"li","s":["6 December (anniversary of the shooting of 15-year-old student Alexandros Grigoropoulos)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some demonstrations in the past have turned violent. Avoid demonstrations wherever possible and move away to the last known safe place. Security forces often use tear gas to break up demonstrations, which can harm your breathing and vision."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thefts of passports, wallets and handbags are common on the metro and in crowded tourist places, particularly in central Athens. Do not carry all your valuables in one place and keep a copy of your passport photo page somewhere safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving on holiday, keep your valuables out of sight and lock your vehicle at all times. Always park in a well-lit area or secure car park. Be alert to car crime."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk, especially late at night and around clubs and bars:"]},{"k":"li","s":["save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easier to find at the end of the night"]},{"k":"li","s":["set up a WhatsApp group to keep in touch with others in your group"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep an eye on each other’s drinks to make sure they do not get spiked"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not let a friend walk back to their hotel alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not give a drunk person more alcohol"]},{"k":"li","s":[["see TravelAware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/"]," for tips and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use pre-arranged transport or, where they are available taxi-hailing apps such as Uber or Free Now which supply licensed cabs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Report anything that does not feel right to local authorities or hotel or club management."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Racially-motivated attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of visitors experience no difficulties related to their race, but there have been some racially-motivated attacks, particularly in inner-city areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport, to show to the police if they request identification. Police may not accept a copy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greek police will arrest you for any behaviour they find rowdy or indecent, especially where excessive drinking is involved. Some fancy dress costumes may be regarded as offensive and therefore against decency laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["The courts are likely to impose a heavy fine or a prison sentence if they judge the behaviour to be illegal. Your travel insurance may not cover you if you miss flights because of an alcohol-related arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and underage drinking"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to sell or provide alcohol to anyone under 18, any businesses found doing so can face large fines and possible closure. Bars and nightclubs are not allowed to admit or serve anyone under 18, even if accompanied by an adult. Expect age verification checks at points of sale."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a minor is harmed through excessive drinking, or underage intoxication is brought to the attention of local authorities, parents or other accompanying adults as well as those who supplied the alcohol could face legal consequences under general child protection laws."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Greece have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying goods or services"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law restaurants must provide an itemised bill. Make sure you get a receipt for any goods or services you buy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Carrying weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Offensive items like pepper spray or knuckledusters are listed as weapons in Greece. A knife with a blade measuring 10cm or more counts as a weapon, and you need a special licence for any knife that is not made for domestic, professional, artistic or hunting use."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Greece, and civil unions between same-sex couples have been legal since 2015. The age of consent in Greece is 15, this applies to partners of both the same sex and opposite sex. Transgender people are able to change their legal gender. Anti-discrimination and hate speech laws apply to gender identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public attitudes towards same-sex couples vary throughout the country. Couples showing affection in public may be frowned on, especially in rural areas. Attitudes are generally more welcoming in Athens and on many Greek islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Military service"]},{"k":"p","s":["Men aged 19 and above, born to a Greek national, may have military service obligations, regardless of any other nationality they hold. The authorities can stop you leaving Greece until you complete military service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras or approaching sensitive locations"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to approach or take photos or videos of military installations, vehicles or buildings. The authorities will arrest and have prosecuted those doing so. Border areas are also militarily sensitive. If you visit such areas, do not take photos or videos."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Music festivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care of your valuables at festivals or large concerts. Read the ",["festivals in Europe travel checklist","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"]," for more advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and water sports safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year, people drown in the sea and in swimming pools in Greece."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming pools"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children. Keep small children within arms-reach in and around swimming pools, even if they can swim or there is a lifeguard present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming in the sea. Always supervise children and keep small children within arms-reach."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hidden rocks or shallow depths can cause serious injury or death. Do not dive into unknown water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many organised beaches have a flag system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings. A red flag means you must not enter the water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care and get local knowledge if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further tips on ",["ABTA’s swim safe pages","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"]," and ",["Water Safety on Holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local advice if jellyfish are present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only book activities at a licensed water sports centre and before you start:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure the paperwork is completed"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask for a safety demonstration"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you know how to call for help"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more advice, see the website for ",["Safe Water Sports","https://safewatersports.com/"],", a non-profit organisation in Greece that aims to prevent accidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad (ATV) biking and mopeds"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year people suffer serious injury and even death due to accidents involving quad bikes. Make sure you get full instructions and training on their use. If you are not experienced with driving quad bikes proceed with caution as you will be sharing the roads with larger and faster vehicles."]},{"k":"p","s":["To help with costs incurred as a result of quad bike incidents you need specific travel insurance as quad biking is defined as an extreme sport and excluded on many policies. Always read the details of your insurance cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["Insurance sold by the hire company usually only provides third-party cover. It’s likely the company will charge you for any damage to the rental vehicle, and you may face arrest if you do not pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check that you hold the correct driving license for the vehicle you are hiring. Provisional licenses are not valid in Greece for driving or hiring any type of vehicle. If you hire a moped, you need a valid driving licence with at least category A1 – ‘light motorcycle’. Choose a category in accordance with your driving licence and age. Category P, which is valid in the UK for driving mopeds up to 50cc, is not valid in Greece."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the vehicle is in good condition. Drivers and passengers must wear helmets before operating quad bikes and mopeds. Failure to do so may invalidate your insurance. If police stop you, they will fine you and take your licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and exploring nature"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when planning a hike or walk, especially during higher temperatures than you are used to. Trails often lack shade and the quality of route markings can vary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ensure that you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your route beforehand, and consider your limitations in distance and difficulty"]},{"k":"li","s":["check weather forecasts and avoid hiking during the peak hours of sun; pack a hat, sunscreen and plenty of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["wear appropriate footwear for uneven terrain and consider taking a map, GPS and a fully charged phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid hiking alone if you can, and always tell someone where you are going and the route you will take"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not light fires as it is both dangerous and illegal due to the high risk of wildfires."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance covers you for extra costs such as mountain rescue service and helicopter evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If an accident happens or if you become lost, call 112 for the emergency services."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Camping and Motorhome travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece has introduced regulations prohibiting camping in tents and the parking of trailers, semi-trailers, camper vans and motorhomes at archaeological sites, seashores, beaches, edges of public forests and in general public areas. Ensure that you use licensed campsites to avoid fines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Greece, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Greece guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/greece/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Greece. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Greece. If you are tested and found to have more than two-thirds of England’s legal limit of alcohol in your system, you could get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic can be busy, fast and chaotic, especially in the larger cities. Local drivers regularly ignore speed limits, including in built-up areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["When walking roadside, take care when crossing the road and if possible use a pedestrian crossing. Drivers do not always stop at crossings, even though they are supposed to. The green pedestrian crossing signal sometimes allows cars to turn right on to a crossing, so cross with caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Emergency alerts and preparedness"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece can experience extreme natural phenomena such as earthquakes, wildfires, extreme heat and flash floods. To be alerted to events near where you are located in Greece, make sure your mobile phone is set to allow emergency alerts. For instructions on how to do this see:"]},{"k":"li","s":["for iPhones go to Settings > Notifications and enable the ‘Emergency Alerts’ option at the bottom"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Android 11 and higher go to Settings > Notifications > Advanced Settings > Wireless Emergency Alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Samsung devices go to Settings > Apps > Messages > Notifications > Emergency Notifications and enable the ‘Emergency Alerts’ option"]},{"k":"p","s":["This will allow the ",["Greek government’s Emergency Communication Service","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en"]," alerts to reach you. Always keep your phone with you as you will receive alerts according to the location of your phone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consider preparing a grab bag with essentials such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["passports/ID cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["mobile phones and device chargers"]},{"k":"li","s":["money and bank cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["insurance and other important documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["essential medicine and prescription details"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more from gov.uk on what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adverse weather conditions, including floods, can happen quickly. Register for Emergency alerts and follow ",["‘112 Greece’ on X","https://x.com/112Greece"]," for official updates."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of wildfires during the summer season from April to October. Ensure that your mobile phone is registered to receive emergency alerts to be warned of wildfires near your location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. The situation can change quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid starting wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave no litter, especially not glass which is known to start fires"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarettes are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not light barbecues"]},{"k":"p","s":["Causing a wildfire or a forest fire is a criminal offence in Greece – even if unintentional. If you see a fire, call the emergency services on 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you are in or near an area affected by wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow ",["@112Greece","https://twitter.com/112Greece"]," for official updates"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the guidance of the emergency services"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Greek emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact your airline or travel operator who can assist you with return travel to the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, see the ",["Greek Ministry of Climate Change and Civil Protection website","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en/odigies-prostasias/dasikes-pyrkagies"]," (in English)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes and earth tremors in Greece. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["familiarise yourself with safety procedures in the event of an earthquake"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice given by the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Greek emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further guidance on how to prepare for earthquakes, please visit the ",["Greek Ministry of Civil Protection","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en/odigies-prostasias/seismoi"]," (in English) and to see, for anywhere in Greece, where your nearest assembly points are located in case of emergency you can visit ",["mysafetyplan.gov.gr","https://mysafetyplan.gov.gr/"]," (map with text in Greek)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 or 166 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Greece","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Greece","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Greece. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Changes to your routine when travelling, such as later nights, coping with heat and changes to your diet can have an impact on your medication. See the ",["Summer Proof Your Health","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/heat-travel-and-late-nights-how-summer-can-affect-your-medicines-and-how-to-stay-safe"]," campaign for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies across Greece stock a good supply of medicines, but there are strict rules around dispensing certain medicines, including antibiotics. Bring prescription medicines with you and carry a letter from your doctor stating the quantity required during your stay. Keep the medication in the original container with the prescription label. The name on the prescription must match the name on your passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prescriptions for uninsured individuals are only dispensed from:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pharmacies at hospitals"]},{"k":"li","s":["pharmacies registered with the National Organisations for the Provision of Health Services (EOPYY)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to take controlled medicines in Greece, contact the ",["Organisation Against Drugs (OKANA)","https://www.okana.gr/el/information-english"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, contact the Greek National Organisation of Medicines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 0030 213 2040 395 or 0030 213 2040 285 between 1pm and 2pm on weekdays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: clearance@eof.gr"]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Treatment and facilities are generally good on the mainland, but may be limited on the islands. The standards of nursing and aftercare, particularly in the state sector, is not to the usual standard of the UK. The public ambulance service is basic. There are serious shortages of ambulances on some islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are uninsured, you may not be able to get medical treatment or diagnostic tests from private doctors in Greece, only from public hospitals and primary healthcare centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English. On some Greek islands, local staff in bars or airports may direct you to private first aid or medical centres rather than to the public hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["information if you’re hospitalised in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Greece, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-greece"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["Mental health support for British nationals in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/greece-mental-health-support-abroad/mental-health-support-for-british-nationals-in-greece"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Calling 999 from a UK mobile in Greece will automatically transfer you to the Greek emergency services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Greece"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Greece"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Greece"]," in Greece"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/greece-prisoner-pack/information-pack-for-british-prisoners-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/greece/british-embassy-athens"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-greece"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":27968,"change":"New information about winter weather in Greece, including flash flooding ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/us-demands-that-iraq-disarms-brigades-misread-the-nations-complicated-security-landscape-293491":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"6cdbb1eda6f86b314ea2962206e4e8824803b3b54a6c6a4c9d1091584df05940","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-demands-that-iraq-disarms-brigades-misread-the-nations-complicated-security-landscape-293491","bytes":184394,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US demands that Iraq disarms brigades misread the nation’s complicated security landscape","by":[{"n":"Yasir Kuoti","r":"Ph.D. Candidate in Political Science, Boston University"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T13:41:52Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Iraq marked Sovereignty Day on Sept. 30, 2026, by holding a four-day ",["national holiday","https://www.haaretz.com/middle-east-news/2026-10-02/ty-article/.premium/as-iraq-celebrates-u-s-withdrawal-its-struggle-for-sovereignty-only-begins/000001a0-f906-d9ab-abfd-ffa7bf470000"]," in celebration of the departure of U.S-led international forces. American troops, by far the largest contingent, had been stationed there since 2014 as part of an 87-member coalition that ",["provided Baghdad with military","https://www.inherentresolve.mil/who-we-are/"]," and intelligence assistance. Their leaving was seen as a vital step in Iraq’s transition to sovereign security."]},{"k":"p","s":["The day was also set to mark another development toward that end: the ",["establishment of a “state monopoly” on arms","https://www.newarab.com/news/iraq-extends-armed-groups-disarmament-deadline-june-2027"]," aimed at neutering, in particular, Iranian-backed armed groups that have proliferated since the U.S invasion of Iraq in 2003."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Iraqi government missed its target date. Instead, the deadline has now been ",["pushed back","https://www.newarab.com/news/iraq-extends-armed-groups-disarmament-deadline-june-2027"]," to June 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an ",["expert on Iraqi politics and security","https://www.bu.edu/polisci/profile/yasir-kuoti/"],", I fear that this initial delay portends a wider problem. The Iraqi government is ",["facing increasing pressure from the U.S.","https://www.newarab.com/news/trump-warns-baghdad-over-iraqi-militias-joining-us-iran-war"]," to bring Iranian-aligned armed actors under control. As recently as early November 2026, President Donald Trump ",["reportedly warned Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi","https://www.newarab.com/news/trump-warns-baghdad-over-iraqi-militias-joining-us-iran-war"]," of consequences – financial penalties or potential direct strikes against such groups – should disarmament not happen."]},{"k":"p","s":["But Washington and Baghdad appear to be on different pages when it comes to establishing a so-called state monopoly on the arms. For Iraq’s government, it means pulling some armed groups further within the orbit of the ",["Popular Mobilization Forces","https://carnegieendowment.org/middle-east/research/2017/04/the-popular-mobilization-forces-and-iraqs-future"],", or PMF – a state-sponsored umbrella of armed actors. The U.S, meanwhile, clearly envisions something very different: the demilitarization of armed groups and likely a fundamental reorganization of the PMF itself. Behind that disconnect is a seemingly irreconcilable difference of how both see the role of the Iraqi state."]},{"k":"h","s":["Blurred lines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dozens of armed groups, including those that are Iranian-aligned, currently make up the patchwork of security forces across Iraq’s decentralized political landscape. Some of these have a relationship with the Iraqi state that is complicated and subject to change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2014, many have operated under the umbrella of the PMF. Formed largely in response to the threat from the Islamic State group, the PMF ",["consists of around 60-70 brigades","https://www.fpri.org/article/2026/03/militias-and-iraqs-role-in-regional-conflict/"],", mainly Shiite Muslim groups but with some representing the country’s significant Sunni Muslim minority as well as other ethnic groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["The PMF is formally and legally affiliated with the state and is seen as an Iraq-centered entity – that is to say, it is answerable to the Iraqi prime minister and tasked with providing national defense and regional security as a legal part of the nation’s security apparatus. But in reality, some elements of the PMF operate with a degree of independence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The PMF exists alongside so-called resistance groups – armed groups that are ideologically allied with Iran and often support the aims of Tehran beyond the goals of the Iraqi nation. These include, among others, the Hezbollah Brigades and al-Nujaba Movement – both of which ",["trace their lineage","https://www.washingtoninstitute.org/policy-analysis/profile-asaib-ahl-al-haq-0"]," to the Mahdi Army formed, with ",["Iran’s assistance","https://doi.org/10.1080/23311886.2025.2606371"],", during the U.S. invasion in 2003."]},{"k":"p","s":["The aims of the PMF and those of the resistance groups are not always synonymous. Some resistance groups operate outside of the PMF, while others, such as ",["Asab Ahl al Haq Brigades","https://mappingmilitants.org/profiles/asaib-ahl-al-haq#narrative"],", have units both in the PMF and the outside resistance."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s a complex picture, and the line demarcating the resistance and the PMF is often blurred."]},{"k":"h","s":["Demands from Washington"]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. has long protested the presence of all resistance groups in Iraq. In October 2025, then-U.S. Special Envoy to Iraq Mark Savaya ",["warned that","https://amwaj.media/en/media-monitor/tensions-soar-as-pentagon-chief-issued-final-warning-to-iraq-over-armed-groups"]," “there is no place for armed groups operating outside the authority of the Iraqi state.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of Washington’s concern is the role that some resistance groups have played in attacks on U.S. assets in Iraq and the region. Since hostilities broke out between the U.S. and Iran in February 2026, Iraqi-based resistance factions have launched hundreds of rocket strikes against ",["American forces in Iraq","https://www.arabnews.jp/en/middle-east/who-are-the-iraqi-groups-involved-in-the-middle-east-war-166262"],". They have also attacked ",["infrastructure in Arab Gulf states","https://www.stimson.org/2026/iran-aligned-militias-jeopardize-iraqs-gulf-reset/"]," and targets ",["within Israel","https://israel-alma.org/the-islamic-resistance-in-iraq-attacks-against-israel-november-2-2023-to-november-20-2024/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such attacks prompted the U.S in April to ",["criticize Baghdad for failing","https://iq.usembassy.gov/security-alert-u-s-embassy-baghdad-iraq-april-2-2026/"]," to “prevent terrorist attacks in or from Iraqi territory” by “Iran-aligned terrorist militia groups [who] claim to be associated with the Iraqi government.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iraq under al-Zaidi, too, wants ",["an end to groups on its soil joining Iran","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/6/iraqs-al-zaidi-talks-to-trump-as-baghdad-seeks-to-stay-out-of-war-on-iran"]," in retaliation strikes against the United States and its allies. But the U.S. and Iraqi governments seemingly differ on how."]},{"k":"p","s":["Washington appears to want the dismantling or meaningful restructuring of armed groups writ large. But al-Zaidi’s plan simply seeks to bring the ",["resistance factions","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/who-are-iraqs-iranian-backed-armed-groups-2026-07-29/"]," into ",["the state-sanctioned PMF","https://nesa-center.org/csag-strategy-paper-irans-shadow-army-the-pmfs-growing-influence-in-iraq/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["And on this front, some progress has been made. On Oct. 6, al-Zaidi ",["marked the halfway milestone","https://www.alaraby.co.uk/politics/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B2%D9%8A%D8%AF%D9%8A-3-%D9%81%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%84-%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%85%D9%86-%D8%A3%D8%B5%D9%84-5-%D8%B3%D9%84%D9%91%D9%85%D8%AA-%D8%A3%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%87%D8%A7"]," of this “state monopoly of arms” by announcing that he had convinced three out of the five main resistance factions sitting outside the PMF to surrender their weapons to the state, with negotiations ongoing with the other two. By the “state,” al-Zaidi almost certainly means the ",["PMF Commission","https://understandingwar.org/research/middle-east/the-leadership-and-purpose-of-iraqs-popular-mobilization-forces/"]," – the official state body that administers, funds and oversees the PMF."]},{"k":"h","s":["The messy business of state formation"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Washington, that may not be sufficient. More than a century ago, sociologist Max Weber famously ",["defined the state","https://www.jstor.org/stable/pdf/20006938.pdf?refreqid=fastly-default%3A6e4c9ab347679605b284e7a1c21013b3&ab_segments=&initiator=&acceptTC=1"]," primarily as a means to centralize rulemaking and monopolize the use of legitimate violence – and this view prevails in Western nations."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in Baghdad, the state is deliberately a ",["communalized entity","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/unfinished-business-nation-building-in-iraq-since-2003/"]," in which armed groups operate within the legal framework, if often nominally, to carry out the work of security forces. It reflects the nation’s multiethnic and sectarian makeup."]},{"k":"p","s":["Herein lies much of the problem in reconciling the U.S. and Iraqi governments’ view of what a “state monopoly of arms” means."]},{"k":"p","s":["To Washington, al-Zaidi’s idea of refashioning the resistance more firmly under the auspices of the PMF, while leaving the underlying arms and effective command structures intact, appears insufficient."]},{"k":"p","s":["But anything more would be a tall order. Individual armed groups within the PMF are deeply embedded in the structure of the nation’s political order; members sit in and dominate parliament, hold cabinet positions and control state bureaucracy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Asking the government to disarm these groups would first require that Iraq’s leaders conceive of the state in an entirely different way. Some observers have warned that it ",["could lead to civil war","https://www.kurdistan24.net/en/story/932410/badr-warns-disarming-iraqi-armed-groups-could-trigger-civil-war"],", while the leader of at least one of the armed groups has ",["already accused al-Zaidi","https://alhurra.com/en/53406"]," of “implementing an American agenda.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Not many modern nations possess the communal security apparatus that defines Iraq today. But this security landscape is a fact of post-2003 Iraq, and it is unlikely to be going away anytime soon."]}],"chars":6777},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T17:20Z","sha":"c76aee699826e97a4354b1b00ee5aa95e1dbfc7f04195be691dc707ab254b4c1","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/qatar","bytes":71164,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Qatar travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-31T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-18T16:32:02+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure. There remains a risk of further attacks across the region at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Qatar’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Qatar set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, ",["contact Qatar’s embassy in the UK","https://london.embassy.qa/en/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Qatar, your passport should be valid for at least 6 months from the date you arrive. You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a resident of Qatar, your passport must be valid when you arrive."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a tourist visa on arrival if you’re travelling on a full British Citizen passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must still get a visa in advance if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you’re travelling for any purpose other than tourism"]},{"k":"li","s":["you hold ",["another type of British passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality/british-subject"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to stay longer than 30 days, you must extend your visa waiver before it expires through the ",["Qatar Ministry of Interior","https://portal.moi.gov.qa/qatarvisas"],". If you do not do this, you may be fined. The fine must be paid before leaving Qatar."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is more information on visa requirements and extensions on the ",["Qatar Ministry of Interior website","https://portal.moi.gov.qa/qatarvisas"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are subject to a travel ban, involved in legal proceedings, have unpaid debt or are a child subject to a custody dispute, you may be prevented from leaving Qatar by the Qatari authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transit passengers"]},{"k":"p","s":["At the airport, all bags are scanned. Transit passengers found with even residual amounts of drugs may be arrested. This includes drugs which may be legal in other countries, but not in Qatar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers cannot stay in the transit area for more than 24 hours between flights, even if you are booked into the transit hotel in the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is more information about transit through Qatar on the ",["Hamad International Airport website","https://dohahamadairport.com/airport-guide/at-the-airport/transfers"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mandatory health insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying in Qatar for more than 30 days, you must buy health insurance from a ",["registered Ministry of Public Health ( MOPH) insurance provider","https://www.moph.gov.qa/english/derpartments/policyaffairs/hfid/hirs/insurancecompanies/Pages/default.aspx"]," before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more guidance see the ",["MOPH website.","https://www.moph.gov.qa/english/derpartments/policyaffairs/hfid/Pages/Health-Insurance-Scheme.aspx"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard insurance premium is 50 Qatari riyals per person, per month."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Qatar, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccination in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/183/qatar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about what goods you can take into and out of Qatar. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import and sell vapes and electronic cigarette products. This includes the sale and purchase of related liquids and other similar products, including electronic shisha pipes. The law applies regardless of quantity and intended use. Customs officials may confiscate any such items from your luggage or from packages sent by post."]},{"k":"p","s":["Qatar also prohibits the importation, sale and purchase of electronic cigarettes, liquids and other similar products, including electronic shisha pipes. The law applies regardless of quantity and intended use. Customs officials may seize and confiscate any such items from your luggage or from packages sent by post."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking medication into Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Qatar has ",["guidance on medications","https://london.embassy.qa/en/services/travelling-to-qatar"]," that you can bring into Qatar. For further information on the legal status of a specific medicine, ",["contact the Qatari Embassy in the UK","https://london.embassy.qa/en/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money, precious metals or gems into Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are taking money, precious metals or gems worth more than 50,000 Qatari riyals into Qatar, you must complete a declaration form. This includes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["currency – Qatari riyal or foreign currencies"]},{"k":"li","s":["travellers cheques, money orders, cheques, promissory notes (including those endorsed without restriction, incomplete, payable to a fictitious payee or signed but without the payee’s name)"]},{"k":"li","s":["precious metals – such as gold, silver, platinum"]},{"k":"li","s":["precious stones – such as diamonds, emeralds, rubies, sapphires, pearls"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also give customs officials any other information they request."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you break these rules, you could be fined or imprisoned, as well as the funds or goods being seized."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Qatar cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists issue statements threatening to carry out attacks in the Gulf region. These include references to attacks on western interests, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["residential compounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["military sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["oil"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport and aviation interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants and hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["mosques"]},{"k":"li","s":["large demonstrations"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Events in the region, including political developments, have an impact on local public opinion. Be aware of local sensitivities on these issues. Follow news reports and avoid public gatherings and demonstrations. There is the potential for increased tension on Fridays."]},{"k":"p","s":["If any incidents occur, monitor local media reports and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low, but take sensible precautions to protect yourself and your belongings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Female visitors and residents should take care when walking or travelling alone, particularly at night. Always use pre-booked taxis from reputable taxi companies or recognised taxi apps. Check the registration number and confirm that the driver has your name. Let someone know you are on the way and give them the registration details of the car."]},{"k":"p","s":["Personal attacks, including sexual assault and rape, are relatively rare, but do happen. Qatari law places a high burden of proof on the victim to demonstrate that sexual relations were not consensual. If the court determines sex was consensual, the victim or attacker may still face prosecution for the offence of sex outside of marriage."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have been sexually assaulted, contact the British Embassy in Doha on 00 974 4496 2000. You can also read our ",["guidance for victims of rape or sexual assault in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/qatar-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/guidance-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault-in-qatar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Qatar is an Islamic country. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not cause offence, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or when visiting religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Religion is a sensitive topic in Qatar, approach any discussions with care. You could face imprisonment for defaming, desecrating, or committing blasphemy against Islam, Christianity or Judaism. Public worship and proselytising by non-Islamic faiths is illegal and can result in deportation or imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry your passport as an official form of identification. A copy is usually acceptable, but in some situations you may have to produce the original at a police station within a specified time limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Qatar, your residence card is acceptable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress modestly in public, including while driving:"]},{"k":"p","s":["*men and women should cover their shoulders and knees * the dress code is strictly enforced in government buildings, healthcare facilities and banks - you may be asked to leave or be denied entry"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates change every year. Ramadan in Qatar in 2026 will likely start on 17 February and will last approximately 30 days. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only licensed hotels, restaurants and bars can sell alcohol. Expatriates living in Qatar can get alcohol on a permit system. Don’t carry alcohol around with you (except to take it on the day of collection from the warehouse to your home). The legal drinking age in Qatar is 21. Places serving alcohol will ask for original photo IDs (copies are not accepted) upon entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol or be drunk in public. For example, if you drink in a non-licenced public place, you could get a prison sentence of up to 6 months or a fine up to 3,000 Qatari riyals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships outside marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Any intimacy in public, between any couples (including between teenagers), can lead to arrest."]},{"k":"p","s":["Couples living together while unmarried is illegal in Qatar. Sex outside marriage is illegal for both same-sex and opposite-sex couples. You can be arrested and punishments can include a fine, a custodial sentence and deportation once the sentence is complete."]},{"k":"p","s":["Because of laws on sex outside marriage, if someone becomes pregnant outside marriage, both partners could face imprisonment or deportation. Doctors will ask for proof of marriage during antenatal checks."]},{"k":"p","s":["An unmarried woman who gives birth in Qatar may also face problems registering the birth of the child in Qatar, and could be arrested, imprisoned or deported. To get a birth certificate from the Qatari authorities, you must provide a marriage certificate. Authorities may compare the marriage date against the estimated date of conception."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Qatar. See our ",["information and advice page","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]," for the LGBT+ community before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Organisers of protests need to get permission from the Ministry of Interior. This must be done in advance and cannot be spontaneous."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swearing and rude gestures"]},{"k":"p","s":["Swearing and making rude gestures are considered obscene acts. You can be jailed or deported. Take particular care when dealing with police and other officials."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking is prohibited in all closed public spaces including educational institutions, healthcare facilities, public transport, malls, restaurants and government buildings."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to vape or use an e-cigarette. Police can arrest you and courts can impose a fine, a prison sentence or deportation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is zero tolerance for drugs-related offences in Qatar. Some medications that are legal in other countries are illegal in Qatar. See ",["guidance on medications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar/health#bringing-medication-into-qatar"]," that you can bring into Qatar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for using, trafficking, smuggling and possessing drugs, including cannabis, (even residual amounts) are severe."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long prison sentence, deportation and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Qatar have highly effective technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras, binoculars and drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of cultural sensitivities when filming or photographing. Taking pictures and sharing any visual imagery of people without their consent can lead to imprisonment or a fine of up to 100,000 Qatari riyals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some visitors attempting to film or photograph near religious, military, government or construction sites have been arrested. If in doubt, seek permission."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drone use, including aerial photography and filming, is regulated in Qatar. You may need licences or permits before importing or operating a drone. Breaching drone regulations may result in fines, imprisonment and confiscation of equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the latest requirements with the relevant Qatari authorities before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Journalistic activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["Journalists must get permission from the Qatar News Agency (QNA) to film or photograph as part of their work and enter the country on a visiting press permit. Even with permission to film or photograph, you cannot capture or share imagery of individuals without their consent. This permit allows you to take technical equipment like cameras through airport customs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict privacy laws in Qatar. See ",["the guidelines for using cameras and binoculars","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar/safety-and-security#using-cameras-and-binoculars"],". Posting messages, videos or photos that appear to insult or slander people, or are culturally insensitive, may be considered a crime. Individuals have been detained, prosecuted and convicted for posting this type of material."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Financial crimes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial crimes include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["fraud"]},{"k":"li","s":["giving somebody a cheque which bounces (including post-dated and ‘security’ cheques)"]},{"k":"li","s":["non-payment of bills (for example hotel bills or car hire)"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also be liable for cheques that you have signed on behalf of a company."]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial crimes can be punished with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["imprisonment"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel ban"]},{"k":"li","s":["fines"]},{"k":"li","s":["deportation"]},{"k":"li","s":["freezing bank accounts and other assets"]},{"k":"li","s":["seizing of any end-of-service benefits or bonuses"]},{"k":"li","s":["blocking your access to possible future sponsors (employers)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have unpaid loans or financial commitments you may be prevented from leaving Qatar."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more details about ",["financial crimes if you are living and working in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-qatar#finance"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Qatar, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not have a Qatari driving license, you’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["To drive for longer than 6 months you’ll need to ",["apply for a Qatari driving licence","https://hukoomi.gov.qa/en/service/apply-for-new-driving-license"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving regulations"]},{"k":"p","s":["The driver and front seat passenger must wear their seat belts at all times. It is illegal to use a mobile phone while driving - you could be fined 500 Qatari riyals."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drink and drive, and there is zero tolerance for it. Driving under the influence of any amount of alcohol is punishable by a prison sentence of between one month and 3 years or a fine of 10,000 to 50,000 Qatari riyals, or both. Offenders may also be deported."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even minor expressions of ‘road rage’ like rude gestures can attract significant penalties. You may be:"]},{"k":"li","s":["fined"]},{"k":"li","s":["imprisoned"]},{"k":"li","s":["deported"]},{"k":"li","s":["banned from leaving the country until your case has been resolved – serious cases may take up to 6 months to be heard"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the ",["Metrash2 app","https://portal.moi.gov.qa/metrash2/en/index.html"]," before trying to leave the country, which lists any outstanding traffic violations. If you have an outstanding violation, you could be detained at immigration and denied onward travel. Fines for all violations should be settled in full before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road discipline is very poor; speeds are high and accidents are common. A driver flashing their lights can mean they are coming through rather than giving way."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, it’s illegal to leave the scene of the accident without reporting it on the METRASH application, but if no one has been injured and it’s safe to do so, you can move your vehicle to a safer place. You’ll need to get a police report for insurance purposes. Accident investigation processes and punishments for violations may be different to the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Desert drives"]},{"k":"p","s":["Excursions to the desert can be hazardous unless in a properly-equipped 4x4 vehicle. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in convoy with other cars"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a supply of water and a mobile telephone"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave travel plans with friends or relatives"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your vehicle has the correct insurance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling by dhow. The safety of these vessels may not be up to UK standards. Make sure life jackets are available."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many areas of the Gulf are highly sensitive, including near maritime boundaries and the islands of Abu Musa and the Tunbs in the southern Gulf. Vessels entering these areas have been detained and inspected, and there have been occasional arrests. Make careful enquiries before entering these waters or visiting ports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional tensions may also affect your route. Vessels operating in the Gulf of Oman, Northern Arabian Sea, Gulf of Aden and Bab El Mandeb regions may be at increased risk of ",["maritime attack","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel, check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company promptly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Qatar","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/183/qatar#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Qatar","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/183/qatar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bringing medication into Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some prescribed and over-the-counter medicines may be controlled substances in Qatar. If you need to bring controlled or prescription medication into Qatar, make sure you follow the steps required by the Qatar Ministry of Public Health, including carrying a prescription and medical report in English or Arabic containing details of your medication and treatment, issued within the last 6 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ministry of Public Health (MOPH) provides an ",["electronic service","https://fli.moph.gov.qa/?lang=en"]," which enables travellers arriving to the State of Qatar to submit applications for permits allowing them to carry controlled medicines for personal use, with the ability to track their applications and receive permits online."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities in Qatar are similar to those in the UK. Visitors will be required to pay for medical treatment. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation to the UK or the country where you live. Read more about ",["what your travel insurance should cover","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/qatar-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Qatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?serviceType=lawyers&country=qatar"],", and ",["translators and interpreters in Qatar","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Qatar"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/coping-with-death-abroad-qatar"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/qatar-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re in ",["hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/qatar/british-embassy-doha"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/qatar/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Qatar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-qatar"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23390,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (See ‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/togo":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"566739b9d941201a5572bbbb3155ad26d6ba0cbed87da291b7e102ad3fb96183","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/togo","bytes":47555,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Togo travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-04T16:27:18+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Togo-Burkina Faso border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 30km of the border with Burkina Faso, except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the city of Dapaong and the N1 highway leading to it from the south."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Savanes Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the rest of the Savanes region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/togo/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/togo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Togo’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Togo set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Togolese High Commission in the UK","https://togohclondon.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the date you plan to leave Togo."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a resident in Togo, your passport must be valid for 6 months from the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Togo. A single-entry tourist visa is valid for 15 days. You must apply for a visa at least 5 working days before you plan to arrive in the country. You cannot get a visa on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer (or to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons), you must ",["meet the Togolese government’s entry requirements","https://voyage.gouv.tg/about"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply and pay for an e-visa","https://voyage.gouv.tg/"]," to visit Togo."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling through Togo"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a visa if you’re travelling through Togo. For layovers in Togo’s airports, it is advisable to check with the airline on whether a transit visa is required."]},{"k":"h","s":["Online registration certificate"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["fill in a registration certificate online","https://voyage.gouv.tg/about/procedures"]," before you arrive in and depart from Togo."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Togo, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccines, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Togo guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/222/togo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Togo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Togo."]},{"k":"p","s":["The main threat in Togo is from Jama’at Nusrat al-Islam wal-Muslimin (JNIM) and other al-Qa’ida (AQ) affiliated groups, including al-Qa’ida in the Islamic Maghreb (AQIM). JNIM is mainly active in the northern region of the country near the Burkina Faso border. However, attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["beach resorts"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["cafés and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases and security installations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist kidnapping is infrequent in Togo, but may occur. FCDO advises against all travel to within 5km of the border with Burkina Faso, due to the security situation in Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political rallies, protests and violent demonstrations can take place unexpectedly. Monitor media outlets, updates from the local authorities or from your travel operator about possible disruptions. Be vigilant if you’re visiting crowded public places or attending events which attract large crowds. If you see a threatening or intimidating situation, stay away and exercise caution. Turn around and move to safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cities of Sokodé, Bafilo and Mango have a history of violent demonstrations where protesters and security forces have been injured and killed. If you’re in an area of any town or city when a demonstration happens, leave immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Togo-Burkina Faso border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 5km of the border with Burkina Faso, due to the security situation in Burkina Faso and the risk of kidnapping in the region."]},{"k":"h","s":["Togo’s other borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Togo’s borders can close at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime, theft and pickpocketing are common in Togo, particularly on the beaches and markets of Lomé. Attacks take place during the day and at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can protect yourself and your belongings by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not travelling alone, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["not carrying valuables or large amounts of cash with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["making sure purses and bags are closed and not easy to grab"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have also been reports of carjackings. Armed criminals may stage a traffic accident so they can flag down vehicles."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scam artists target foreign visitors and residents. The scams come in many forms – romance and friendship, business ventures, work and employment opportunities – and can cause financial loss. Warn your friends and family to be sceptical if they’re asked to transfer funds to you in Togo. Tell them to contact you to check you’ve made this request."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry a copy of the photo page of your passport with you at all times. Make sure you’re able to access the original quickly if needed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs is a serious offence and can result in fines and a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to take photographs of or near sensitive or official sites such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["military installations"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["airport buildings"]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual relationships are illegal in Togo and penalties are severe. You could be fined or given a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Togo is a cash-based society so bring enough cash with you to cover your visit. Credit cards are not widely accepted. Some hotels and restaurants will accept credit cards, but card-paying machines are not reliable so you may be asked to pay in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some ATMs in the capital, Lomé, accept international cards and dispense local currency."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ocean currents are very strong along the coast and there are a number of drownings each year. Dangerous beaches are unlikely to have warning signs. Follow local advice before swimming."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Togo, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Togo for up to 6 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying for longer than 6 months, you’ll need get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Togo. There are no set blood alcohol content limits, but if traffic control officers suspect you of drink-driving they can order a medical exam. Punishments range from a fine and a prison sentence of one to 3 years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads outside towns and cities are poorly lit. During the rainy season, minor unpaved roads may be blocked."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may encounter official and unofficial roadblocks. Stop at control points if asked. Turn on your interior vehicle lights and only continue when you’re told you can."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards in Togo are poor and add to the risk of accidents. Public transport vehicles can be poorly maintained and are often driven over the speed limit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of piracy and armed robbery against large vessels in Togolese waters and those of neighbouring countries. Mariners should take appropriate precautions. If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 8200 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest information on ",["vaccination recommendations for Togo","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/222/togo#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Togo","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/222/togo"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to go to a pharmacy to buy most over-the-counter medicines. They are not sold in supermarkets in Togo. Where possible, buy known brands. Pharmacies are widely available and are usually identified by a green cross. They will usually accept prescriptions from the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Togo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are poor. Emergency facilities are extremely limited. For serious medical treatment, medical evacuation may be necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Togo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 8200"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 117 or 177"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=togo"]," in Togo"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Togo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/togo-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Togo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/togo-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/togo/british-high-commission-accra"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/togo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":13205,"change":"Updated information about applying for a visa (see 'Visa requirements' on the 'Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/us-schools-are-moving-away-from-ai-in-google-searches-should-australia-do-the-same-297160":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T20:53Z","sha":"2cfc55a054a7a72dc584860670feeb5f7fd268af17c3c8f84b6050d1ff895aa9","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-schools-are-moving-away-from-ai-in-google-searches-should-australia-do-the-same-297160","bytes":178475,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US schools are moving away from AI in Google searches. Should Australia do the same?","by":[{"n":"Miriam Tanti","r":"Deputy Dean Commercial Growth and Professor of Education and Co-Director, La Trobe AI Institute, La Trobe University"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T19:10:04Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Three major school districts in the United States are contemplating ",["moving away from Google search engines","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/18/technology/google-gemini-ai-search-schools-nyc-la-chicago.html"],", so students are not forced to use artificial intelligence (AI) in their daily school work."]},{"k":"p","s":["The New York Times has reported that teachers, parents and US government officials in Los Angeles, New York City and Chicago are worried Google’s embedded AI tools will impact students’ learning."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, should Australian schools follow suit?"]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s happened?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier this month, ",["Google said","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/09/parents-teachers-google-search-schools-ai"]," that schools choosing to impose a complete ban on Google’s AI tools will also have to ban Google Search."]},{"k":"p","s":["The tech giant ",["claims","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/03/us/google-search-schools-restrict-ai.html"]," this is because its AI tools, such as the AI overview at the very top of search results, are so “deeply integrated” into search functions that the AI software can’t be switched off. Teachers and parents were unimpressed by this response."]},{"k":"p","s":["Google’s search function and other standalone AI tools, such as its AI chatbot, Gemini, will be automatically switched off for students from next year, with school administrators having the option to turn them back on."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a post published to X on November 4, News from Google states:"]},{"k":"p","s":["We know there’s concern about students using AI to shortcut schoolwork, and schools have told us they want control. That’s exactly why we are making these changes today to address the feedback we’ve heard from educators in recent months."]},{"k":"p","s":["Still, this does not give schools an AI-free version of Google Search."]},{"k":"h","s":["How AI in searches affects learning"]},{"k":"p","s":["When students are given an AI summary as part of online searches it can potentially result in them ",["bypassing critical thinking","https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2025.1550621"]," and research skills when ",["developing their digital literacy","https://doi.org/10.1177/0961000619898213"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For instance, when students use online search engines without AI assistance, they must learn to choose appropriate search terms, decide which websites to trust, evaluate different viewpoints and trace claims back to original sources."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Australia’s most recent national digital literacy test, which assesses, among other skills, students’ ability to find and judge information online, ",["only 37% of Year 10 students","https://theconversation.com/only-37-of-year-10-students-meet-our-national-standards-for-digital-skills-283759"]," reached the expected standards – the lowest score since testing began in 2005. This suggests more work needs to be done in building Australian students’ digital literacy skills."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another important point to consider is tech companies’ influence on students’ learning. When AI is integrated seamlessly into applications schools already use, the company’s design choices can shape what happens in classrooms. This includes when and how students encounter AI."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s happening in Australian schools?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Google is already used in many Australian classrooms. Public schools in ",["New South Wales","https://education.nsw.gov.au/technology/products-and-services/software/googleworkspace"],", ",["Victoria","https://arc.educationapps.vic.gov.au/software/26"]," and the ",["Australian Capital Territory","https://www.act.gov.au/education-and-training/life-at-school-and-college/technology-in-act-public-schools"]," can all access Google’s education tools through their local departments of education."]},{"k":"p","s":["Google’s ",["website states","https://knowledge.workspace.google.com/admin/getting-started/editions/control-access-to-google-services-by-age?hl=en"]," AI Overview is available to school users under the age of 18 in most countries."]},{"k":"h","s":["How should AI be used in schools?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s ",["framework for generative AI in schools","https://www.education.gov.au/schooling/resources/australian-framework-generative-artificial-intelligence-ai-schools"]," says:"]},{"k":"li","s":["AI should be used in ways that support and enhance students’ critical thinking"]},{"k":"li","s":["teachers should design assessments that clearly outline how AI should or should not be used."]},{"k":"p","s":["The complexity arises when teachers ask students to not use AI in a particular assessment. Teachers might want to see evidence that students have located and evaluated sources without AI assistance. But when students search Google, the AI overview is the first thing they see."]},{"k":"h","s":["Is Australia’s new digital detox the answer?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier this month, state and federal education ministers ",["agreed to restrict students’ use of generative AI","https://theconversation.com/australian-classrooms-are-getting-a-digital-detox-what-does-this-mean-for-schools-and-students-295951"],", such as ChatGPT, in primary schools and high school assessments."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ministers ",["recognised","https://www.education.gov.au/download/20853/digital-detox/46397/document/pdf"]," students are engaging with AI not just when using education software, but also “through search engines, social media, and other online platforms they use every day”."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the digital detox doesn’t outline any specific standards about students encountering AI through search engines, social media or other applications – leaving a gap in guidance."]},{"k":"h","s":["What next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["England’s approach to AI in education can offer clues on how to help students use AI without it doing the work for them. The British government asks makers of education AI tools to not give students answers or full solutions until ",["they’ve had a go","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/generative-ai-product-safety-standards/generative-ai-product-safety-standards#cognitive-development"]," at answering questions on their own. This is part of a new mandate that has set certain standards for educational technology companies to meet. Although it may take some time to see the impact in classrooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s ",["recommendations","https://st4s.edu.au/the-rai-standard/"]," for companies that develop educational software do not go into specifics about how they should protect student learning, which they should."]},{"k":"p","s":["But agreeing on national standards for student learning isn’t simply a question of switching AI off or keeping it on. Sharing insights across school systems could reveal which tools genuinely improve learning, helping teachers everywhere effectively integrate AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["Working closely with teachers, tech companies can build AI tools that protect and develop students’ thinking, while teaching them how to use AI well. But the decision about when a child uses AI should always be a deliberate one made by the teacher who knows that child – not a tech company."]}],"chars":5195},"https://theconversation.com/trump-had-4-reasons-to-convince-nvidia-to-rehire-jensen-huang-heres-why-it-matters-globally-297377":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T21:39Z","sha":"49b933afaad0c64ff688e49b1b9ee64520b9881dbec0560c73bcd63e19f17f8a","read":"https://theconversation.com/trump-had-4-reasons-to-convince-nvidia-to-rehire-jensen-huang-heres-why-it-matters-globally-297377","bytes":181889,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Trump had 4 reasons to ‘convince’ Nvidia to rehire Jensen Huang. Here’s why it matters globally","by":[{"n":"Marta Khomyn","r":"Senior Lecturer, Finance and Data Analytics, Adelaide University"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T04:57:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Just 11 days after resigning as chip maker Nvidia’s chief executive, Jensen Huang has been rehired by the company he co-founded, vowing “I’m going to be ",["a better CEO the second time around","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=unawbXKdSZI"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The company’s board said its unexpected, unanimous decision came after “input from senior levels of the United States government”."]},{"k":"p","s":["US President Donald Trump went even further, declaring in an interview that he “convinced them” to bring Huang back. The company had ",["bluntly ruled out Huang’s return","https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/articles/nvidia-shuts-down-jensen-huang-093453815.html"]," just days ago."]},{"k":"p","s":["But why would a US president meddle so openly in ",["the world’s second-most valuable company","https://www.tradingview.com/news/stocktwits:058e52ebe094b:0-nvidia-is-now-second-to-apple-in-the-world-s-most-valued-companies-on-jensen-huang-optimism/"],"? And why does the leader of Nvidia matter beyond the US – including the speed at which data centres are built worldwide?"]},{"k":"h","s":["A trillion-dollar turnaround"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia’s stocks plunged after Huang announced his resignation on November 12, following reports of extramarital affairs, one with a woman identified by US intelligence as being ",["in touch with China’s top spy agency","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/22/us/politics/alice-huang-china-spy-agency-nvidia.html"]," and another with an Nvidia employee. Both raised concerns about Huang’s judgement as CEO."]},{"k":"p","s":["Allegations of previously publicly belittling staff – including ",["a senior executive who temporarily succeeded him as CEO","https://www.wsj.com/tech/jensen-huang-colette-kress-nvidia-ceo-eb289097"]," – have also been reported by the Wall Street Journal and New York Times."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia’s stock ",["closed at US$174","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/crypto/articles/jensen-huang-back-nvidia-could-181650969.html"]," a share on November 11, the day before Huang quit. Within eight days, the share price had fallen to about US$126, knocking as much as US$1.2 trillion off its market value – and dragging down the wider US share market."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the day of Huang’s return, the company’s shares surged 31% to US$165, pushing its market valuation back up by ",["nearly US$1 trillion","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nvidia-adds-nearly-1-trillion-221300670.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s behind Trump’s ‘extraordinary’ intervention?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The relationship between the US government, Nvidia and other tech companies has become really entangled."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even so, it’s extraordinary for a president to have called one of the world’s most valuable companies and told its board to reinstate the CEO. It’s hard to imagine any president other than Trump doing that."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an economist, I think in terms of incentives. On Nvidia, I believe Trump had four main incentives to weigh in."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, there’s the obvious economic impact of Nvidia’s falling share price on the wider US stock market."]},{"k":"p","s":["Asked if last week’s AI selloff was a factor in his push to reinstate Huang as CEO, ",["Trump said","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/trump-admits-falling-stocks-pushed-193215456.html"],": “Probably so, but the bigger impact was the long term.” Trump added “I made the deal” and that his intervention was “very important” to Huang’s return."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then there’s a political incentive."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s been growing talk in the media in recent months about the “ ",["AI bubble","https://theconversation.com/is-the-ai-bubble-about-to-burst-what-to-watch-for-as-the-markets-wobble-270113"],"” bursting. The wobbles in AI stocks became especially noticeable when Nvidia lost about one-third of its market capitalisation after Huang’s resignation."]},{"k":"p","s":["All of those losses threaten the perception that markets do well under Trump – ",["a claim","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/trump-made-stock-market-marker-success-now-hedging-markets-dip-rcna195704"]," he’s long made."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Trump’s intervention in Nvidia is extraordinary by historical standards, it’s not the first time his administration has significantly intervened in the market."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Trump, the US government last year took a ",["10% stake in Intel","https://www.intc.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1748/intel-and-trump-administration-reach-historic-agreement-to"],". It has also ",["bought 10–15% stakes","https://www.mining.com/web/trump-backed-critical-minerals-deals-face-growing-pressure-after-blue-wave/"]," in other tech-related companies, especially miners of critical minerals needed for AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["The success of AI and tech-related mining companies has become inextricably tied to this administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then there’s a personal incentive."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Financial Times reported","https://www.ft.com/content/67b0a070-c2a9-4229-885a-383cca657763?syn-25a6b1a6=1"]," the surge in Nvidia’s share price on Monday could have made Trump between US$1.3 million and US$15 million. That’s based on his most recent financial disclosures, which show Trump may have owned as many as 370,000 shares at September 30."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, there’s Trump’s personal relationship with Huang."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s been reported he takes Huang’s advice on all things AI to a significant extent, both in private and in public. For instance, ",["Huang recently took a phone call","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-10/trump-phone-call-interrupts-nvidia-ceo-s-panel-discussion-/107368390"]," from Trump while on stage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Huang has been one of the few AI industry leaders who hardly mentions potential downsides of AI. Trump has shunned mentions of AI doomsday scenarios or the need for greater safety."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why does this matter globally?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Huang, Nvidia has become ",["the central bank of AI","https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/nvidia-insists-it-can-keep-printing-money-to-fund-the-ai-boom-195e7d5e?mod=article_inline"],": fuelling the AI boom, both with its advanced chips and its funding of tech firms that need those chips."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia is a cash-rich company, with enormous profit margins."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many well-known tech companies that buy Nvidia chips, such as Anthropic and OpenAI, are still comparatively cash poor. They have ",["huge spending commitments","https://theconversation.com/was-anthropics-record-us-81-billion-listing-a-vote-of-confidence-in-ai-and-whats-next-297151"]," and need someone to fund them. The companies then use the money Nvidia provides as an investor to buy Nvidia chips. The better they do, the more chips they buy – and the better Nvidia does."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia has also been a crucial investor in data centres, providing ",["US$228 billion","https://about.bnef.com/insights/data-centers/nvidias-228-billion-data-center-bet-three-things-to-know/"]," in guarantees, leases and investments for data centre providers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Who’s paying whom? The circular money machine behind the AI boom (or bubble)","https://theconversation.com/whos-paying-whom-the-circular-money-machine-behind-the-ai-boom-or-bubble-293938"]]},{"k":"p","s":["But what happens if investors lose confidence in AI? Nvidia’s “circular financing” arrangements mean it’s extremely exposed to the AI industry overall, both on the data centre side and among the AI companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["After Huang resigned, Nvidia’s chief financial officer, Colette Kress, was appointed as interim CEO."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kress – ",["who’s staying on as CFO","https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director"]," – has reportedly been an important counterweight to Huang on risky financing deals. According to several media outlets, Kress ",["renegotiated a proposal","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/cfo-colette-kress-just-made-012602987.html"]," for Nvidia to provide US$250 billion in guarantees for an OpenAI data centre in Ohio, instead cutting that commitment in half."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, Kress is not universally opposed to circular financing. In August ",["she publicly defended","https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/nvidia-insists-it-can-keep-printing-money-to-fund-the-ai-boom-195e7d5e?mod=article_inline"]," Nvidia’s approach, saying “we know some will call this circular financing. We see it differently”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Why does that history matter? Because if Kress or someone other than Huang had been CEO, investment in AI might have slowed. That would have real-world impacts well beyond the US, including how quickly data centres expand worldwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Huang has been the world’s best known salesman of AI. Now that he’s back as CEO, his incentives – like Trump’s – are the same as before his resignation. Hype up AI’s future, shut down criticism of it and keep the circular finance flowing."]}],"chars":6098},"https://theconversation.com/50-years-of-the-sex-pistols-not-agents-of-chaos-but-dreamers-of-a-utopia-296476":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-25T21:22Z","sha":"b10c8e1606422343dd7021af1879c14ff74060af0cd69108f5012cb45564538b","read":"https://theconversation.com/50-years-of-the-sex-pistols-not-agents-of-chaos-but-dreamers-of-a-utopia-296476","bytes":183663,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"50 years of the Sex Pistols: not agents of chaos, but dreamers of a utopia","by":[{"n":"John Schofield","r":"Associate Professor, Archaeology, Flinders University; University of York"},{"n":"Paul Graves-Brown","r":"Research Associate, Department of Archaeology, University of York"}],"pub":"2026-11-25T19:07:32Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["On November 26 1976, a London-based punk band released a record that created shock waves around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["While not the first punk single to be released (The Damned’s ",["New Rose","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ThcXEqxI_IQ"],", Radio Birdman’s ",["Burn my Eye","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2i3RIpKXGp0"]," EP, and ",["I’m Stranded","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWeX65b5dOk"]," by the Saints were released a few weeks earlier), ",["Anarchy in the UK","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cBojbjoMttI"],", by the Sex Pistols set the tone and a high bar for what was to follow."]},{"k":"p","s":["With its snarling lyrics (“I am an antichrist”) and raw sound, the song blew a gaping hole in 1970s complacency."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Sex Pistols are often thought to be obnoxious anarchists who promoted chaos. But in many ways they were the opposite."]},{"k":"p","s":["Here are five ways they created a template for a more inclusive, more tolerant, and better balanced society that remains relevant in today’s uncertain world."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. Social and political convention"]},{"k":"p","s":["Like many parts of the developed world, Britain in the mid-1970s faced ",["economic decline","https://lordslibrary.parliament.uk/the-uk-economy-in-the-1970s/"],", industrial unrest and growing disillusionment with established institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anarchy in the UK, followed by the band’s next single, God Save the Queen, released during Queen Elizabeth II’s Silver Jubilee in 1977, voiced the anger and alienation of many people while raising questions about national authority and identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pistols opened a door for many young people, inviting them to ",["challenge established regimes","https://faroutmagazine.co.uk/sex-pistols-anarchy-in-the-uk-song-meaning/"],", and to say no."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their assertion that there was “ ",["no future","https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2011/nov/23/sex-pistols-graffiti"],"” is also relevant today."]},{"k":"h","s":["2. Style and fashion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alongside their strong influence on music, the Pistols heavily influenced style and fashion."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is sometimes claimed the Pistols were conceived as a vehicle for ",["Vivienne Westwood’s","https://www.theviviennefoundation.com/vivienne/"]," iconic clothing, which included bondage wear. As well as wearing her clothes, the band also took their name from her shop ",["SEX","https://gatamagazine.com/articles/sex-vivienne-westwoods-legendary-store"]," on Chelsea’s Kings Road in London."]},{"k":"p","s":["Westwood’s punk stylings encouraged others to create distinctive clothes and outfits from everyday and discarded items, including bin-bags and safety pins."]},{"k":"p","s":["Based on her work with the Sex Pistols, and their manager Malcolm McLaren, Westwood’s career as a fashion iconoclast continued until her death in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elsewhere, graphic designer ",["Jamie Reid","https://www.artnet.com/artists/jamie-reid/"],"’s combination of “ransom note” typography and situationist style détournement has had a lasting effect on graphic art and design, while the filmic work of ",["Julien Temple","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMq31VLA3_g"]," (who made the Sex Pistols 1980 film The Great Rock ‘n’ Roll Swindle) has heavily influenced the development of the rock biopic."]},{"k":"h","s":["3. DIY"]},{"k":"p","s":["One of the Pistols main influences was in the emergence of a DIY approach to music."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is perhaps epitomised in the Pistols ",["infamous gig","https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/4f0B5rf6z2wYQpm5WNqsqP7/they-swear-they-were-there-sex-pistols-at-the-lesser-free-trade-hall"]," at the Lesser Free Trade Hall in Manchester on June 4 1976, which inspired attendees to form their own bands (famously: Joy Division, Buzzcocks and The Smiths)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this, the myth that the Pistols “couldn’t play” simply inspired the realisation that anyone could pick up a guitar and make a record."]},{"k":"p","s":["This DIY approach also involved the dissemination and promotion of music and the artists, through home-made ",["fanzines","https://sniffinglue.co.uk/pages/about"],", the precursor to the blogs and zines that proliferate today."]},{"k":"h","s":["4. Gender and inclusivity"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pistols encouraged women to become musicians."]},{"k":"p","s":["Siouxsie Sioux was a member of the Pistols entourage, the Bromley Contingent, contributing to the chaos of the Sex Pistols’ infamous ",["TV confrontation with Bill Grundy","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OC16gG5Rtzs"]," before founding the Banshees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Palmolive and Viv Albertine of the ",["Slits","https://www.bing.com/videos/riverview/relatedvideo?q=Slits&&mid=7FC3EC2F21026C5619A47FC3EC2F21026C5619A4&churl=https%3a%2f%2fwww.youtube.com%2fchannel%2fUCfM-3hDSJkd2M_YGSn8oVkw&FORM=VRDGAR"]," were previously members of the (unrecorded) Flowers of Romance along with John Ritchie (aka Sid Vicious). Chrissie Hynde, who had worked at SEX, went on to form The Pretenders. Poly Styrene was inspired to form ",["X-Ray Spex","https://www.bing.com/videos/riverview/relatedvideo?q=X+Ray+Spex&&mid=913B710E32D62CE4526D913B710E32D62CE4526D&churl=https%3a%2f%2fwww.youtube.com%2fchannel%2fUC57ov99ruLVkQTskhRqK9Ow&mmscn=stvo&FORM=VRDGAR"]," having seen an early Pistols gig in Hastings in 1975."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pistols were central to a London punk scene that embraced and promoted diversity and difference at a time of racial tensions and intolerance."]},{"k":"h","s":["5. Global influence"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pistols soon found fans across the world, including in many countries in the ",["Soviet orbit","https://sonicaekrano.pt/en/punk-under-communist-regime/"],", where their anti-establishment pronouncements found a resonance among disaffected youth."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Indonesia, the circulation of semi-legal cassette tapes, and the few music publications tolerated by President Suharto’s “ ",["New Order","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Order_(Indonesia)"],"” ultimately inspired an anarcho punk scene typified by Bandung band ",["Runtah","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gag7P9Iqnt4"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thriving punk scenes have developed across the globe from Brazil to Japan, from Australia to the Arctic."]},{"k":"p","s":["At a downtown bar in Perth, Australia, decades after the Sex Pistols first performed, another punk band rattle through their electrifying and energetic set to an adoring and enthusiastic audience. Pogoing may have evolved into moshing, but otherwise much remains the same."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Amyl and the Sniffers","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0mlOh_oSils"]," are among the latest in a long line of bands from around the world to have embraced the spirit of punk and the Pistols, carrying the legacy to a new generation of audiences."]},{"k":"p","s":["This article draws on ",["The Routledge Handbook of the Sex Pistols","https://www.routledge.com/The-Routledge-Handbook-of-the-Sex-Pistols/Dines-Gelain-Graves-Brown-Schofield/p/book/9781032788371"],", edited by the authors with Mike Dines and Gabriela Gelain."]}],"chars":4834},"https://theconversation.com/apa-jadinya-jika-hakim-menggunakan-ai-dalam-memutus-perkara-295968":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T05:07Z","sha":"20685c62517b9a034e90c6bf0969c787a35ab46668064e8d3f2ce5418c901c06","read":"https://theconversation.com/apa-jadinya-jika-hakim-menggunakan-ai-dalam-memutus-perkara-295968","bytes":180423,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Apa jadinya jika hakim menggunakan AI dalam memutus perkara?","by":[{"n":"Shevierra Danmadiyah","r":"Peneliti, Indonesian Institute for Independent Judiciary (LEIP)"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T04:17:45Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Penggunaan akal imitasi oleh hakim berisiko melanggar privasi data pribadi."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Bias algoritma dan sifat ruang gelap teknologi mengancam independensi serta akuntabilitas hakim."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Teknologi seharusnya sebatas alat bantu yudisial, bukan menggantikan nalar kritis penegak hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pernahkah kita membayangkan saat berperkara di pengadilan, hakim memasukkan segala informasi terkait perkara kita ke dalam platform akal imitasi (AI), seperti ChatGPT, Claude, DeepSeek, dan Gemini, dengan prompt permintaan pembuatan putusan?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penggunaan AI oleh hakim bukan lagi imajinasi semata. Pada 2023, ",["hakim di Kolombia","https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/feb/03/colombia-judge-chatgpt-ruling"]," menuai kontroversi karena memasukkan transkrip tanya-jawabnya dengan ChatGPT dalam putusannya terkait perkara asuransi bagi anak dengan autisme."]},{"k":"p","s":["Praktik senada juga terjadi di yurisdiksi lain, seperti di ",["Afrika Selatan","https://legalbrief.co.za/diary/legalbrief-africa-new/story/acting-judge-accused-of-using-ai-to-prepare-ruling-4/"]," dan ",["Inggris","https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/sep/15/court-of-appeal-judge-praises-jolly-useful-chatgpt-after-asking-it-for-legal-summary"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi hakim, penggunaan AI mungkin hanyalah persoalan efektivitas dan efisiensi dalam bekerja, sehingga mereka mampu memproduksi lebih banyak putusan setiap hari. Namun, bagi pihak yang berperkara dan bagi publik, penggunaan AI oleh hakim bukan hanya soal putusan yang diproduksi hakim, melainkan soal bagaimana keadilan yang nantinya akan mereka terima."]},{"k":"h","s":["Risiko penggunaan AI oleh hakim"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terdapat beberapa potensi masalah krusial apabila hakim memutus perkara dengan bantuan AI."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. Risiko pelanggaran privasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Saat hakim memasukkan informasi terkait perkara ke dalam AI, bisa jadi terdapat data pribadi yang turut disetorkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di titik inilah, hakim-hakim sedang mensuplai informasi, termasuk data pribadi, ke perusahaan-perusahaan teknologi raksasa. Praktik ini melanggar privasi pihak yang berperkara karena data pribadinya dibagikan oleh hakim kepada perusahaan teknologi raksasa tanpa seizinnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, hal demikian bertentangan dengan prinsip hak atas privasi, khususnya pelindungan data pribadi, sebagaimana dijamin ",["Undang-Undang Perlindungan Data Pribadi","https://www.datahukum.com/peraturan/UU_27_Tahun_2022.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Perlukah menghilangkan jejak digital? Ada dilema dalam menyeimbangkan hak atas privasi dan hak atas informasi","https://theconversation.com/perlukah-menghilangkan-jejak-digital-ada-dilema-dalam-menyeimbangkan-hak-atas-privasi-dan-hak-atas-informasi-242923"]]},{"k":"h","s":["2. Mengganggu independensi hakim"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penggunaan AI oleh hakim dalam memutus perkara berpotensi mengganggu independensi hakim yang seharusnya tidak bisa ditawar-tawar dalam lembaga peradilan. Independensi merupakan nilai sentral dalam ",["Prinsip Bangalore","https://www.unodc.org/pdf/crime/corruption/judicial_group/Bangalore_principles.pdf"]," dan ",["Kode Etik dan Pedoman Perilaku Hakim (KEPPH)","https://kepaniteraan.mahkamahagung.go.id/images/artikel/kode%20etik%20dan%20pedoman%20perilaku%20hakim%20ma%20ky.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perlu disadari bahwa informasi yang ditampilkan oleh AI tidaklah netral, melainkan bergantung pada data yang diinput dan dilatih. Secara faktual, bias masih terus melekat pada AI."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian","https://researcher.manipal.edu/en/publications/assessing-bias-in-large-language-models-a-comparative-study-of-ch/"]," mengenai bias sosial dan gender mengungkapkan: ChatGPT masih seringkali bias, Gemini terkadang bias dan terkadang tidak, serta Claude masih menunjukkan bias dalam porsi yang kecil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam ",["riset lainnya","https://www.ucl.ac.uk/news/2024/dec/bias-ai-amplifies-our-own-biases"],", jika seseorang terus-menerus berinteraksi dengan sistem AI yang bias, hal ini dapat menjadikan ia semakin bias."]},{"k":"p","s":["Risiko tersebut sekaligus membantah anggapan bahwa penggunaan AI akan menjadikan hakim semakin obyektif dan bebas bias."]},{"k":"h","s":["4. Akuntabilitas yang tidak jelas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika hakim memutus menggunakan AI tanpa meninjaunya kembali, ada risiko pelanggaran akuntabilitas karena ‘melempar’ tanggung jawab ke suatu teknologi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, dalam memutus perkara, menurut ",["Transparency International","https://files.transparencycdn.org/images/TI_Policy_Position_Judiciary_02.07.pdf"],", hakim dituntut untuk bersikap akuntabel. Dengan menggunakan AI, besar kemungkinan hakim tidak bisa bertanggung jawab atas apa yang menjadi luaran AI karena hakim tidak mampu mengikuti alur pemikiran dari sebuah keputusan AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["Inilah yang dimaksud dengan ruang gelap AI (the black box nature of AI)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Menyingkap “black box” AI di balik permainan naik turun tarif ojek online","https://theconversation.com/menyingkap-black-box-ai-di-balik-permainan-naik-turun-tarif-ojek-online-243587"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Istilah “black box” dalam konteks AI ini pertama kali diperkenalkan sejak 2015 oleh pakar hukum Amerika Serikat, ",["Frank Pasquale","https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=3884360"],". Pasquale menggunakan istilah ini karena bermakna ganda: perangkat perekam di satu sisi, dan di sisi lainnya, merujuk pada operasi misterius di dalam suatu sistem."]},{"k":"p","s":["Makna ganda tersebut memberikan gambaran tentang bagaimana sistem AI merekam—melalui pengumpulan data—serta memproses data tersebut dengan caranya sendiri."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sejauh mana batas hakim memakai AI?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Praktik di beberapa negara menunjukkan bahwa memutus perkara adalah wilayah yang tidak boleh dipengaruhi oleh AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di ",["pengadilan Singapura","https://www.kas.de/documents/278334/38385073/AI+in+the+Judiciary+KAS+Report.pdf/a8f6a7bb-ca1a-0500-472f-3b0f1ba8e8b1?version=1.0&t=1758862022674"],", AI tidak digunakan untuk pengambilan keputusan karena dinilai masih terdapat isu mengenai keterjelasan, bias, dan akuntabilitas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Taiwan, publik mengkritik sistem pembuatan draf putusan berbasis AI karena dinilai berpotensi mencederai keadilan prosedural dan mengikis peran hakim. Di Eropa, ",["Komisi untuk Efisiensi Peradilan (CEPEJ) (2018)","https://www.coe.int/en/web/cepej/cepej-european-ethical-charter-on-the-use-of-artificial-intelligence-ai-in-judicial-systems-and-their-environment"]," mempertimbangkan bahwa penggunaan AI semestinya dikesampingkan untuk tujuan penciptaan norma berbasis kuantitas putusan yang nantinya dapat memengaruhi hakim memutus perkara di masa mendatang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, AI telah digunakan di lingkungan peradilan, salah satunya melalui Smart Majelis milik Mahkamah Agung (MA) untuk membantu penunjukan majelis hakim. Namun, penggunaannya masih berbeda dari AI generatif untuk menyusun analisis atau putusan perkara."]},{"k":"p","s":["MA juga mulai membahas batas penggunaan AI oleh hakim, mulai dari penggunaan untuk administrasi hingga hal-hal yang berisiko mengambil alih fungsi inti hakim, seperti menilai bukti dan menentukan putusan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia perlu mempertegas aturan penggunaan AI di peradilan, terutama terkait pelindungan data pribadi, verifikasi hasil AI, transparansi, dan akuntabilitas. AI seharusnya hanya menjadi alat bantu, bukan pengganti nalar kritis dan tanggung jawab hakim."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada akhirnya, putusan adalah produk utama pengadilan yang di dalamnya harus mencerminkan nilai-nilai keadilan dan HAM."]},{"k":"p","s":["AI tidak boleh menggantikan pemikiran dan analisis hakim. Penggunaan AI dalam sistem peradilan harus ditempatkan hanya sebagai alat bantu dalam mengakselerasi fungsi-fungsi yudisial, yang meliputi perlindungan HAM, penyeimbang cabang kekuasaan yang lain, dan penegakan independensi peradilan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Secara spesifik, penggunaan AI ini juga harus memerhatikan berbagai prinsip penggunaan yang telah disepakati seperti di Eropa, ",["ASEAN","https://cacj-ajp.org/cacj-activities/publications/governance-framework-on-the-use-of-ai-for-the-asean-judiciaries/"],", dan ",["UNESCO","https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/ai-courtroom-unescos-new-guidelines-judiciary"],". Prinsip-prinsip tersebut pada dasarnya meliputi empat aspek utama, yakni perlindungan terhadap HAM; keamanan sistem; transparan, akuntabel, dan keterjelasan; serta pengawasan dan pengambilan keputusan oleh manusia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Bagaimana jaksa dan kepribadian hakim pengaruhi tingginya vonis?","https://theconversation.com/bagaimana-jaksa-dan-kepribadian-hakim-pengaruhi-tingginya-vonis-111983"]]}],"chars":6270}};
